    {
      "body": "/tag-and-rerun-ci",
      "created_at": "2026-04-28T04:50:53Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/23895#issuecomment-4332434174",
      "id": 4332434174,
      "updated_at": "2026-04-28T04:50:53Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "yhyang201"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Superseded by #43960.\r\n\r\nTwo notes on why this needed a fresh PR rather than a rebase here:\r\n1. `filter_batch(v1_spec_info_filtered=True)` no longer exists on main — the current signature is\r\n   `filter_batch(chunked_req_to_exclude=None, keep_indices=None)`.\r\n2. The trigger is broader than `return_logprob=True`: the `else` branch of\r\n   `_get_new_batch_prefill_raw()` is taken whenever `is_mixed_chunk` is False, and\r\n   `is_mixed_chunk = chunked_prefill_size is not None and enable_mixed_chunk` with\r\n   `enable_mixed_chunk` defaulting to `False`. So this reproduces with the default config\r\n   (verified: `#running-req` ramps 0 -> 31 for a 256-request chunked-prefill run while the\r\n   client-side in-flight is 16; after the one-line fix it stays at 0-1, throughput unchanged).\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-13T02:48:17Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/23895#issuecomment-6137098988",
      "id": 6137098988,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-13T02:48:17Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "hope1262946533"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks @yhyang201! This is covered on main now: #44351 drops finished requests from the running batch on every scheduling step, before admission, which includes the non-mixed prefill path that `return_logprob` falls into. The `filter_batch(v1_spec_info_filtered=True)` call here also no longer matches the current signature. Closing as superseded; please reopen if I've missed a case.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-15T03:56:28Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/23895#issuecomment-6184040240",
      "id": 6184040240,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-15T03:56:28Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "hnyls2002"
      }
    }
